{
  "summary": "Escapes embedded newline characters as '\\x0a' in the logging subsystem via BCLog::LogEscapeMessage. Strips any single trailing newline from log messages before escaping and appends the final newline centrally in Logger::Format. Adds functional tests verifying that newlines in rejected RPC method names and wallet paths cannot forge new log lines in debug.log.",
  "problem": "Untrusted user inputs like rejected RPC method names or wallet names can contain unescaped newline characters. Restricted RPC users or callers can exploit this to inject forged log entries into debug.log, potentially misleading node operators or automated log monitoring tools.",
  "evidence": [
    "PR description provides a concrete reproducer where an unauthorized RPC call to 'getblock\\n<fake error>' successfully injects an 'ERROR: ConnectTip: ConnectBlock ... failed' line into debug.log"
  ],
