  "changed_since_previous": "Dropped the util::SplitLines helper and the updates across multiline logging call sites (exceptions, UI messages, wallet diagnostics), keeping only the core logger escaping change and functional tests.",
  "card": "This pull request prevents user inputs from forging log lines in debug.log by escaping embedded newlines as hex sequences in the logging subsystem. Currently, inputs such as rejected RPC method names or wallet paths preserve newlines through log escaping, allowing restricted RPC users to inject fake entries that appear to come from the node. The author demonstrates this with a reproducer injecting a fake block connection error into debug.log. Trailing newlines from existing log calls are stripped before escaping and re-appended centrally to avoid altering normal single-line formatting.",
